{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Secret Valentine", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Say It in Rhymes", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 13, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " What is a poem?", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " A poem is a piece of writing that is nearly always rhythmical, and often has elements such as meter, rhyme, and stanzas.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You write poetry to express your thoughts and ideas in a shorter form.<br /><br /> Sometimes, the end of each line can rhyme.<br /><br /> Here are some terms that you use when describing poetry.<br /><br />", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">  Word </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">  Definition </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"rhyme\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" one of two or more words or phrases that end in the same sounds\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" stanza\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" a group of lines in a poem\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" meter\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" a way of arranging the sounds or beats in poetry \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" rhythm\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" a regular, repeated pattern of sounds or movements\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Oh, I wish that you were mine.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I think about you all the time.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modals for Suggestions, Necessity, and Possibility", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use modals when you want to express possibility, suggestions and necessity.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">may</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span> and <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to express possibility in the past and in the future. <br />*<span class=\"italic\">Might</span> suggests that something is less possible than<span class=\"italic\"> may</span>. <br /><br /> <ul> \t<li>might / might not + infinitive</li> <li>could / could not + infinitive</li> <li>may / may not + infinitive</li> </ul> Example: <br /> <span class=\"italic\">You might be able to speak with him before work.</span><br /> <span class=\"italic\">You could be kind and friendly when you approach him.</span><br /><br /> <span class=\"strong\">Should, could, might</span> and <span class=\"strong\">would </span> are used to express suggestions:</span><br /><br /> Example: <br /> <span class=\"italic\">You should be direct with him.</span><br /> <span class=\"italic\">That would be the best way to handle the situation.</span><br /><br /> The modal verbs <span class=\"strong\">must</span>, <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">have got to </span>show that something is necessary.<br /> <span class=\"strong\">Must</span> is the strongest of the three and is most common in writing. <br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\">It <span class=\"strong\">must</span> be very hard for him to speak to you.</span><br /> <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> let him down softly.</span><br />", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "a long-lost relative", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person you have not seen or heard from in a long time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  It might be from a long-lost relative.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in a conversation between friends.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to calm down", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to relax; to reduce anxiety", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Calm down and let me see. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to let someone down", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to decline someone's interest", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I hope you let him down easily.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rhyme ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "one of two or more words or phrases that end in the same sounds", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The poem even rhymes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "stanza ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a group of lines in a poem", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are three stanzas in the poem.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type